  "notes": [
    "The anchor and 0x52cdb80f are the attacker's stake-release cycles that planted duplicate ORN liability entries; the drain by a second attacker EOA relied on them. The 13 earlier successful requestReleaseStake calls since 2021 were by accounts without an ORN liability, so none exercised the defect.",
    "Loss is the exchange's outflow in the drain (every asset sent out, including 79.9 native BNB), net of the 4M USDT flash deposit and of the attacker's own 1 USDT and 0.3 ORN deposited in the referenced setup txs. The ORN token admin burned the attacker's ORN 1.5 h later; recoveries are not netted.",
    "The Feb 2023 Orion record (eip155:56:0xfb153c57…) is a depositAsset reentrancy in an older implementation, a different vulnerability, so it is not merged."
  ],
